For large separation $r_{12}:=\|\vec{r}_2-\vec{r}_1\|\gg\alpha$, $\gamma_{1,2}$ are the only minimal (or extremal) surfaces; as $r_{12}$ is increased, they approach the spheres $\|\vec{r}-\vec{r}_i\|=\alpha$ (see Fig.\ \ref{fig:2 ER}). The minimal surface homologous to the sphere at infinity in region $a_3$ is $\gamma_1\cup \gamma_2$.

