\kappa_{g_{1/2}(D)}(x,x') = \kappa_{f(D)}(x,x').
\]
On the right hand side, we note that  the finite-propagation methods from \cite{Higson00}, in particular Proposition 10.3.5, used in the proof of Proposition \ref{prop kernel decay}, apply to bounded Borel functional calculus, so also to the distributional kernel of $f(D)$. 

