\end{table}

We apply the high-quality event selection from the previous section to the dataset described in section~\ref{sec:dataset}. This selection yields 40 high-quality hybrid events with energies reconstructed by the SD between \SI{3.4(7)}{EeV} and \SI{12.6(12)}{EeV}. The number of events remaining after each cut is detailed in Tab.~\ref{tab:event_selection}. The most restrictive cut is the minimum \Eem threshold of \SI{4}{EeV} as reconstructed by AERA, which corresponds to the threshold for full efficiency of the SD for inclined events. Given the high energy of the selected events, the large footprint of the radio emission on ground for inclined showers, and the dense layout of AERA, the hybrid detection with SD and AERA is also expected to be fully efficient.

