Virtual Network Embedding (VNE) is central to network virtualization. Given a set of requests for instances of virtual networks, VNE requires to map a maximum number of these requests to an underlying physical network, subject to capacity constraints. Each node in a virtual network instance represents a virtualized function and each link represents communication between the two functions. A solution to VNE maps each virtual function to a physical node and each virtual link to a path in the physical network. 
