\begin{lemma}
    Suppose that the inclusion $A_{i}\subset N_{i,0}$ is $(A_{i}\subset M_{i})$-nuclear. There exists a weakly nuclear $*$-homomorphism $$\pi\colon \mathcal{T}(\mathcal{H})\to (C^*(N_{1,0}\oplus N_{2,0},T)^{(A_{1}\oplus A_{2})\sharp (A_{1}\oplus A_{2})})^{*}$$ such that $\pi(x) = i_{C^*(N_{1,0}\oplus N_{2,0},T)}(x)$ for all $x\in (A_1\oplus A_2)\cup \tau(\mathcal{H})\cup \tau(\mathcal{H})^{*}$.
