each ${\mathcal F}_i$ is a $\nabla^g$-totally geodesic foliation and by de Rham Decomposition Theorem (see \cite{KN}), $(M,g)$ splits into 
$(\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_k)$-weighed product of
almost Hermitian manifolds.
Now, let the $A$-torsion condition \eqref{Eq-A-T} be true, then
by Theorem~\ref{mainweak}, $(M,g)$ splits into the $(\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_k)$-weighed product of nearly K\"{a}hler manifolds.
\end{proof}

