%proposes to vaccinate DL programs against crashes through automated program transformation. Specifically, to allow a DL program ready for in-situ fixes, \textsc{Daifu} automatically decomposes its essential functions (specified by developers) into several sub-functions (namely cells in this paper) in advance, and instruments code into each cell to fight again crashes. The actual execution of the DL program is then based upon the transformed cells. With this decomposition and instrumentation, the impact of a crash can be restricted within a cell and a local fix is made possible. If the DL program encounters a crash during execution, only the suffering cell will exit, and then the instrumented code will intercept the crash and let the DL program gracefully wait for a fix rather than crash directly. Further, to perform in-situ fixes, \textsc{Daifu} provides two interfaces to manipulate the program state or fix the code of the failed cell. Developers can interact with the failed DL program with these interfaces to repair a crash, or implement automated recovery strategies on the basis of them. Finally, to recover a program after a fix, \textsc{Daifu} synthesize a new cell that constitutes the rest logic of the failed cell with the faulty parts (if exists) corrected. The synthesized cell is entered for the rest execution. 

