	\begin{abstract}
		For a given d-minimal expansion $\mathfrak R$ of the ordered real field, we consider the expansion $\mathfrak R^\natural$ of $\mathfrak R$ generated by the sets of the form $\bigcup_{S \in \mathcal C}S$, where $\mathcal C$ is a subfamily of the collection of connected components of an $\mathfrak R$-definable set.
		We prove that $\mathfrak R^{\natural}$ is d-minimal.
		A similar assertion holds for almost o-minimal expansions of ordered groups.
	\end{abstract}

