\subsection{Dataset Construction}
\label{sec:dataset}
\textbf{Experimental Dataset.} We first extracted all molecules from the original dataset and computed both Tanimoto similarity and cosine similarity between each pair. For each molecule, we selected the top 10 most similar molecules based on each metric, merged the results, and removed duplicates to form the candidate molecule set $M_{cm}$. Each unique query molecule paired with its corresponding $M_{cm}$ constitutes one problem instance. These problem instances were further filtered according to the following criteria:
\begin{itemize}
\item For each query molecule, the number of associated interacting proteins must be between 2 and 10.
\item For each candidate molecule in $M_{cm}$, the number of associated interacting proteins must be between 2 and 4.
\item The total number of candidate molecules per query must not exceed 15.
\end{itemize}

