\subsubsection{Interpreting the Inference Trace}

The explainable trace in Table 2 records every Fixed‐Point Operation (FPO) in one run of the “42” game, showing how PyReason:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item Asserts each drawn card via the \texttt{card\_drawn\_obj} fact at certainty \([1,1]\).  
  \item Fires \texttt{player\_holds} to add the card’s point value \(v\) to the lower bound of \texttt{hand\_as\_point\_vals.}  
  \item Fires \texttt{odds\_of\_losing} to compute the interval \([p,1]\), where \(p\) is the fraction of remaining cards that would push the total above 42.  When \([p,1]=[1,1]\), no safe draws remain and the game ends.
\end{enumerate}




