\section{Scalar field four-point functions}

The total one-loop scalar field 4-correlators $S_{4X}\equiv\big<X^{A_1}X_{A_2}X_{A_3}X^{A_4}\big>$ 
is the sum of the contributions from the sum of diagrams given in Figs.\ref{fig:Fig21}-\ref{fig:Fig4-6tad}
\begin{equation}
S_{4X}=S^{tad}+S^{bub}+S^{tri}+S^{box},
\label{S4X}
\end{equation}
where $S^{box}$, $S^{tri}$, $S^{bub}$ denotes contributions from the eight box, eight triangle, 
and nine bubble diagrams, represented partly in Figs.\ref{fig:Fig21}-\ref{fig:Fig41}, and denoted as:
\begin{equation}
S^{box}=\sum_{r=1}^8 S^{box}_r,\;\;S^{tri}=\sum_{r=1}^8 S^{tri}_r,\;\;S^{bub}=\sum_{r=1}^9 S^{bub}_r.
\label{btb}
\end{equation}
There is also six scalar fields tadpole contribution $S^{tad}$ from a single loop diagram, (up to the $\pi$-,$\sigma$-permutations of all fields in (\ref{AS6})), given in Fig.\ref{fig:Fig4-6tad}, respectively. Number of contributions from (\ref{S4X}) actually do not exists due to the absence of relevant contributing terms in the action $S$ (\ref{Action}). 

