\section{Conclusions}
In previous paper \cite{Martin:2017nhg} we have introduced ABJM  quantum field theory on the noncommutative Moyal manifold and, by using the component formalism, show that it is ${\cal N}=6$ supersymmetric. For the $\rm U(1)_\kappa\times U(1)_{-\kappa}$ case, we have computed all one-loop 1PI two-, and three-point functions in the Landau gauge and show that they are UV finite and have well-defined commutative limits $\theta^{\mu\nu}\to 0$, corresponding exactly to the 1PI correlators of the ordinary ABJM field theory. In this paper we continue with the $\rm U(1)_\kappa\times U(1)_{-\kappa}$ case by using again the component formalism in the Landau gauge.

We compute all one-loop 1PI 4-point functions and show that they are UV finite and have well-defined commutative limits $\theta^{\mu\nu}\to 0$, (\ref{limSbox},\ref{limStria},\ref{Stad1}), corresponding exactly to 1PI correlators of the ordinary ABJM field theory. This result also holds for one-loop correlators which are UV finite by power counting. 

Now note that the effect of UV/IR mixing is present in each tadpole and bubble contributions containing pure tadpole type of integrals (\ref{B.5},\ref{B.37},\ref{C.3}), separately. However we have shown that in the sum of non-planar bubble+tadpole (\ref{I_1+2}) contributions the UV/IR mixing effect cancels out. Also scalar 1-loop triangle $(S^{tri})$, and box $(S^{box})$ diagram contributions to 4-point functions, which are UV finite by power counting rule, in $\theta^{\mu\nu}\to 0$ limit vanish. So considering contributions to the scalar field 4-point functions (\ref{S4X}) in $3D$ from our analysis we see that vanishing in the limit $\theta^{\mu\nu}\to 0$ holds, i.e. that we can write:
\begin{equation}
\lim_{\theta\to 0}\; S^{box}\big|_{(\ref{limSbox})}=\lim_{\theta\to 0}S^{tri}\big|_{(\ref{limStria})}=0 \;\; \&\;\;\lim_{\theta\to 0}\; {(\cal NP)}\big[S^{bub}+S^{tad}\big]_{(\ref{I_1+2})}=0,
\label{S'slimit}
\end{equation}
proving this way vanishing of the sum of the 4-point functions in the commutative limit $\theta^{\mu\nu}\to 0$, for the NCABJM theory (\ref{Action}), i.e.:
\begin{equation}
\lim_{\theta\to 0}\; S_{4X}\big|_{(\ref{S4X})}=0.
\label{S4Xlimit}
\end{equation}
Next, in Sections 6 and 7 we analyse and conclude that vanishing of 2scalar-2(h)gauge and 2scalar-2fermion 4-point functions in the limit $\theta^{\mu\nu}\to 0$ holds. Thus we claim that the NCABJM theory is free from the NC IR instabilities on the level of the 4-point function. 

In Section 8 we discussed limiting properties of the scalar 6-point functions too. Namely we have proven that the limit $\theta^{\mu\nu}\to 0$ of the 1-loop 1PI scalar 6-point functions exists, and that it is equal to 1-loop 1PI scalar 6-point functions of the ordinary U(1) ABJM theory. \\

Summing altogether up by taking into account results from previous \cite{Martin:2017nhg} and this paper, by applying the Lebesgue’s dominated convergence theorem to the Fourier transformed NCABJM theory and by direct computations of relevant loop integrals contributing, we have shown that in the limit $\theta^{\mu\nu}\to0$ of the NCABJM theory all IR divergencies disappear, and that noncommutative ABJM theory,  up to the 1-loop scalar 6-point functions order, flows smoothly to the ordinary commutative ABJM theory. 

$\phantom{XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX}$Q.E.D.\\

