\subsection{Choice of LLMs}
\label{sec:choice_of_llms}
As discussed in Section \ref{sec:solutions}, S3 and S4 depend on external LLMs. In this section, we conduct a detailed investigation into the effects of different LLMs. Beyond recognition performance and flip consistency, we introduce a new metric called \emph{multi-run consistency}, which measures the stability of a model's outputs across multiple runs. As illustrated in Figure \ref{Figure11-1}, S4 shows lower multi-run consistency than S3. These results indicate that the longer reasoning process in S4 tends to produce greater cumulative differences and more varied prediction outcomes. Figures \ref{Figure11-2} and \ref{Figure11-3} demonstrate that Qwen3-14B achieves the highest flip consistency while maintaining competitive recognition performance, highlighting its exceptional capability for preference prediction. Therefore, we select Qwen3-14B as the default LLM in this paper.
