Table \ref{tab:sim_Baker_etal_inference} presents the empirical coverage of $95\%$ confidence intervals for $ES_\text{avg}$. All estimators display correct coverage across all considered DGPs. In terms of inferential precision measured by the length of the $95\%$ confidence intervals, the results once again highlight the practical gains of using our efficient DiD estimator. The relative size of these gains varies with the degree of serial correlation in the data, as expected and consistent with our theoretical results. 


