Recall that $d$ is dimension of covariates $X$. Define for any vector \( k = (k_1, \dots, k_d) \in \mathbb{N}_0^d \) of \( d \) nonnegative integers the differential operator
\[
D^k = \frac{\partial^k}{\partial x_1^{k_1} \cdots \partial x_d^{k_d}},
\]
where \( k. = \sum k_i \). Then for $\alpha>0$ and a function \( f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathbb{R} \), let
\[
\|f\|_{\alpha} = \max_{0 \leq k. \leq \alpha} \sup_x |D^k f(x)| + \max_{k. = \alpha} \sup_{x, y} \frac{|D^k f(x) - D^k f(y)|}{\|x - y\|^{\alpha - k.}},
\]
where the suprema are taken over all \( x, y \) in the interior of \( \mathcal{X} \) with \( x \neq y \). The H\"older space \( \mathcal{C}^{\alpha}(\mathcal{X}) \) of order \( \alpha \) is the space of all continuous functions \( f: \mathcal{X} \to \mathbb{R} \) for which the norm \( \|f\|_{\alpha} \) is well defined and finite. Let \( \mathcal{C}^{\alpha}(\mathcal{X})_M \) be the subset of all functions with \( \|f\|_{\alpha} \leq M \). 
